1.59.m:
Henceforth I shall speak of the cultured (*śiṣṭa*), the good (*sat*), and the virtuous (*sādhu*).
The word *sat* belongs to Brahman; those who possess it [are *santaḥ*];
and through ultimate union with Brahman, they are called the good.

1.61.m:
The Sūta said:
The seers had some business, O best of brāhmaṇas;
having assembled on the crest of Meru, they then deliberated thus.
